// E2E protocol coverage for the default release console (ADR 0125 §1.5/§1.6,
// BT-3575): `mode => release`, `console => true`, `include-compiler = false`
// (the default). Run against its own dedicated release-mode node
// (`e2e_release_mode_console_default_tests`), never the shared workspace-mode
// node `e2e_language_tests` uses.
//
// This file has no `@load` and issues no eval expression that expects
// success: the default release ships no compiler, so `eval` — and so every
// expression below the header, plain or via a `:`-meta command that itself
// evaluates source — is refused with `release_mode_no_compiler` at the
// protocol op gate itself (`beamtalk_capability:classify(<<"eval">>) ->
// compiler`), before any expression is even parsed. This holds regardless of
// *what* the source says: `1 + 1`, a class definition, `SomeClass reload`,
// even `Workspace flush`/`SomeClass removeFromSystem` typed as source — all
// of them are `eval` requests first. Reaching flush/removeFromSystem's own,
// more specific `release_mode_no_workspace` refusal needs `eval` to pass
// this outer gate, which only happens under `include-compiler` — see
// `release_console_include_compiler.btscript`.
//
// What a no-compiler release console *can* still do: `run-entry` (no
// source, no compile — ADR 0125 §1.5/§1.7), `actors`, `sessions`. This file
// also proves `Beamtalk releaseInfo`/`shapeManifest` are reachable this way
// — declared as `class` methods on `BeamtalkInterface` precisely so
// `run-entry`'s class-side dispatch reaches them with no compiler at all
// (`stdlib/src/beamtalk_interface.bt`).
//
// `run_test_file_opts` skips `clear_bindings` for this file — see its own
// doc for why (`Session current clear` is itself an eval, always refused
// here).

// ===========================================================================
// eval (and everything source-shaped) is refused — release_mode_no_compiler
// ===========================================================================

1 + 1
// => ERROR: OTP release

// A `>>` method-patch is source too — same op-level refusal, no need for
// the class to exist (the gate runs before parsing).
BT3575NoSuchClass >> foo => 1
// => ERROR: OTP release

// `:reload <Class>` -> `<Class> reload`, still an eval — same refusal, no
// need for the class to actually exist (the gate runs before parsing).
:reload BT3575NoSuchClass
// => ERROR: OTP release

// ===========================================================================
// run-entry, actors, sessions — always available (ADR 0125 §1.5)
// ===========================================================================

:actors
// => No actors

:sessions
// => _

// `Beamtalk releaseInfo` — a non-release node would answer `#{#release =>
// nil}`; this node *is* a release, so the shape differs (this fixture never
// booted from a real `-boot_var RELEASE_DIR`/systools script — see
// `beamtalk_release:info/0`'s own doc — so it degrades to
// `#{#release => nil}` too here, precisely the "not a release" case, since
// only the answer's *reachability* is under test in this file, not its
// content).
:run-entry BeamtalkInterface releaseInfo
// => _

:run-entry BeamtalkInterface shapeManifest
// => _
